# Project Charter Draft: RCHN Patient Intake and Scheduling System Replacement
**Consultant:** Jesus Reyes
**Role:** Associate Consultant, NovaTech Consulting
**Engagement:** Riverside Community Health Network (RCHN)
**Date:** September 14, 2026
---
## Project Title
RCHN Patient Intake and Scheduling System
---
## Project Sponsor
Riverside Community Health Network
---
## Business Need
The business need addresses problems that the six clinics are having due to an outdated patient intake and scheduling system. The outdated system has caused workflow issues and patients scheduling issues. These issues create a slow work flow environment, increased patient wait time, scheduling errors, and reporting harder for clinic leaders.
---
## Purpose and High-Level Scope
The purpose of the project is to update the current system for all 6 clinics in RCHN by initiating a plan and deploy method that works for the staff. The high-level scope gets more deep into the actual software or any hardware that might be needed for the system. Training may also be part of the high-level scope because it would allow a smooth transition from the old system to the new one.
---
## Success Criteria
Three outcomes that would tell the project sponsor that the project was successful would be the completion of the project training for staff, a deployment with no issues, and improved workflow/scheduling.
---
